# CODEOWNERS — auto-request reviews from listed owners on PRs touching these paths.
#
# Anchored to the v1.1 security-hardening release (G1 in the hardening plan):
# without CODEOWNERS, any contributor (including bot identities with write
# tokens) could land changes in security-critical paths without an automatic
# maintainer review. Combined with the existing `maf-release-watcher`
# direct-to-main lane (intentional design tradeoff, documented in that
# workflow at line 249), a compromise of the bot identity was unbounded by
# review.
#
# To activate the gate, also enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the
# branch protection rule for `main`.
#
# Pattern matching follows .gitignore syntax. The first matching pattern in
# this file (top-to-bottom) wins. Most-specific paths last.

# --- Default: maintainer reviews everything touched ---
*                                       @joslat

# --- Security-critical surfaces (defense in depth — duplicate of default,
#     pinned explicitly so a future contributor's override of `*` cannot
#     accidentally drop these) ---

# MCP server runtime + tool implementations.
/src/maf-autopilot/Tools/                @joslat
/src/maf-autopilot/Scaffolding/          @joslat
/src/maf-autopilot/Commands/             @joslat
/src/maf-autopilot/Prompts/              @joslat
/src/maf-autopilot/Resources/            @joslat
/src/maf-autopilot/Data/                 @joslat

# Roslyn analyzer NuGet — runs at IDE build time in downstream consumers'
# projects; supply-chain critical.
/src/maf-autopilot.Analyzers/            @joslat

# CI surface — workflows execute with elevated tokens (NUGET_API_KEY,
# COPILOT_ASSIGN_PAT, packages:write). A PR that modifies a workflow can
# silently introduce new secret usage or new auto-merge logic.
/.github/workflows/                      @joslat
/.github/scripts/                        @joslat
/.github/CODEOWNERS                      @joslat
/.github/dependabot.yml                  @joslat

# Security documentation — the public commitments + threat model.
/docs/security.md                        @joslat
/docs/security/                          @joslat
/SECURITY.md                             @joslat

# Private hardening notes / release-tracking memos.
/private/                                @joslat
